SC["c4_reveal"]={img:"furnace",
 t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER ELEVEN — THE HALL OF QUIET ASH`)+P(`Inside, the hall is one vast round room, and the floor is a loom.`)+P(`You see it instantly, the way no one else alive could: a great circular weave of soul-threads stretched across a pit of black iron, hundreds of strands, each one faded gold like old straw — and each one, you understand with rising horror, was once a person. Foreign souls. Transmigrators, like you, harvested across forty years, their threads wound into a furnace that drips slow power into a single set of meridians.`)+P(`Elder Kang stands at the loom's center, and in the threadlight you finally see HIM truly: a man-shaped knot of stolen gold, decades overdue for unraveling.`)+P(`“You see it,” he says, genuinely pleased. “None of the others could, at the end. The Loom sends me a weaver at last.”`)+P(`He does not attack. He produces, instead, a book — a ledger, brushwork forty years deep, and turns it toward you open like a merchant displaying silk. Names. Origins you recognize and origins you couldn't dream. Beside each, a column of what that soul's burning purchased: a famine ended, a plague-ward raised, three realms bought for the sect's golden age, the cloud-ring itself renewed. “I am not a glutton,” Kang says mildly. “I am a treasurer. Every coin in this book was spent on the mountain you've grown so fond of. You have eaten in its kitchens.”`)+((G.f.a2_kang_read)?(P(`And you, who read his threads from the tournament stands, can see the entry he isn't showing you: the spider-silk lines running inward, always inward. Treasurers skim. You've audited one before.`)):(""))+((G.insight>=9)?(P(`Standing in a room woven from a hundred stolen Weaves, your understanding catches fire. Patterns within patterns. Fabric within fabric. The door you have been pressing against blows OPEN.`)):(""))+((G.insight<9&&G.insight>=6)?(P(`Horror is also insight. The realm-door you have been pressing against gives way.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Hear the offer he has made a hundred times before.`,do:()=>{if(G.insight>=9){while(G.realm<3)realmUp();if(!G.pats.unravel){learn("unravel","Unravel");note("Read straight off the furnace's own weave.");}}else if(G.insight>=6){if(G.realm<2)realmUp();};},go:"a2c11_offer"}]};

SC["a2c11_offer"]={t:()=>P(`Kang closes the ledger and makes you the offer. He makes it well — forty years of practice — and he makes it to <i>you</i>, fitted like a tailor.`)+((G.f.a1_intent=="home")?(P(`“The door,” he says simply. “You want the door. Child — the furnace IS the door. Where do you imagine the harvested go? Their threads burn here; the burning opens the way between; I have watched a hundred souls go through it, outward, homeward, while the mountain drank the heat of their passage.” He lets that stand. “One soul pays one passage. It need not be yours. Stand with me one season, help me bring in one harvest — some other dreaming foreigner, someone who has built no life here, made no friends, planted nothing — and I will burn the toll and hold the door, and you will walk through it to your porch light.” The terrible thing, the thing you will not forgive him, is that for three full heartbeats you do the arithmetic.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="strong")?(P(`“The ladder,” he says simply. “You've felt it: realms open to understanding, and understanding has a ceiling — one lifetime's worth. I removed my ceiling forty years ago.” He spreads his hands, and the stolen gold in him gleams. “I am offering you the ledger, boy. Heir, not fuel. The furnace needs a keeper who can SEE it; I need a successor; the mountain needs its treasury. Inherit, and Pattern Sage stops being a word at the top of a list you'll die climbing.” The terrible thing is that he means it — you can read sincerity in a man's threads, and his are smooth as poured bronze.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="even")?(P(`“The books,” he says simply. “You of all people. You audited a steward over vegetables — audit ME. One famine ended: forty thousand lives. Price: one soul that fell out of the sky owing this world nothing and owed nothing by it. Show me the column where that trade runs red.” He opens the ledger again, patient as winter. “The basement taught you that everything is paid for by somebody. I am the only man on this mountain honest about the currency. Keep my books with me. Make the spending fair — you'd be the first who ever could.” The terrible thing is that the ledger balances. You check. It balances.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="safe")?(P(`“The door out,” he says simply. “You want to survive. Sensible — it's why you're the first in forty years to walk in here with allies posted at my threshold.” A nod, almost approving, at the night behind you. “So: walk out. Swear silence on your soul-thread — I can bind such an oath, you can see that I can — and go be a clever outer disciple until you die old. The furnace eats dreaming strangers, not careful neighbors. You were never on the menu, boy. The likes of you, we KEEP.” And the door behind you stands open, and the lanterns are still climbing the mountain, and it would be so easy, and you have spent a year learning exactly what this mountain does to people who take the easy arithmetic.`)):(""))+DIV+P(`Granny Sho's voice in your memory, dry as leaves: <i>the only nights it hums.</i> Above the pit, a hundred faded threads hum. One of them, somewhere in the weave, was a girl who glowed to the inside of the day.`)+((G.sho>=3)?(P(`“Wen Suyin,” you say, to the loom rather than the man, and the hall's hum stumbles — one thread among hundreds flaring faintly gold, like a sleeper hearing her name through forty years of dark. Kang's face does something brief and genuinely startled. For the first time tonight, an outcome he didn't tailor.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`“It's going to hurt one of us.”`,go:"c4_boss"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Take the oath. Walk out. Live.`,hide:()=>(G.f.a1_intent!="safe"),go:"a2c11_oath"}]};

SC["a2c11_oath"]={t:()=>P(`You say yes.`)+P(`It's the sensible word, and you watch it land, and you watch Kang smile, and you watch his hands begin the binding — and that's the mistake, his and yours, because an oath is a weave, and you are the only soul under this Heaven who can watch one being tied around his own thread. You see what the knot actually does. Not silence. <i>Leash.</i> The oath-thread runs from your soul to the furnace, and every leash he has ever tied runs the same way, and you understand in one cold drop that the menu and the staff were always the same list.`)+P(`You are already moving when the sigils ignite — but he started his weave first, and the hall's doors seal with a sound like a book closing.`)+P(`“Almost,” Kang says, with real regret, the grave-cold light gathering. “You were almost sensible.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`No more arithmetic.`,do:()=>{G.f.a2_ambush=true;},go:"c4_boss"}]};

SC.c4_boss={combat:"kang",win:"a2c11_breach",lose:"c4_harvested",
 t:()=>P("Kang sighs, almost fond, and the furnace light bends toward him like iron filings to a lodestone. \u201CForty years of harvest,\u201D he says, \u201Cagainst one season of a boy. Let us be quick.\u201D")+
 SYS("FINAL BATTLE OF THE TRIALS. His Soul-Harvest Seal must be broken \u2014 Unravel it mid-form, catch it on a Mirror Lattice, or pay in blood and threads."),
 cstart:()=>{if(G.f.a2_ambush){C.charged=true;C.i=3;clog('<span class="foe">The Seal was forming while he talked \u2014 the ambush opens with the Harvest already falling.</span>');}}};


SC.c4_harvested={img:"harvested",t:()=>'<div class="ending"><h3>ENDING: THE FURNACE</h3>'+
 P("The Seal closes. Your golden thread pulls loose from your body \u2014 gently, just as he promised \u2014 and is wound onto the loom among the hundred faded others.")+
 P("Far away, under another sky, a porch light is still on. The furnace burns very bright for a very long time.")+
 P('<span class="small">But the Loom between worlds remembers its stitches, and a thread once grasped is never wholly lost\u2026</span>')+"</div>",
 c:()=>[{id:"r",l:"Pull the thread back. (Retry the final battle)",go:()=>{if(CKPT)G=JSON.parse(CKPT);else{G.hp=G.maxhp;G.thr=G.maxthr;}return "c4_boss";}},
  {id:"t",l:"Let it end. (Title screen)",go:"start"}]};


SC["a2c11_breach"]={t:()=>P(`Your last knot closes and Elder Kang comes apart.`)+P(`Not like a man dying — like a sleeve unraveling, forty years of stolen gold sloughing off him in spirals until what hits the floor is a withered husk with a black iron door grafted to its chest, swinging open on nothing.`)+P(`And the furnace, master-less, begins to spin apart. A hundred faded soul-threads whip free of the loom, keening, rising through the broken roof-ring like sparks finally let up a flue — free, going wherever the harvested go when the toll is refunded — and under them the pit itself tears loose, raw hoarded qi slewing toward the dragon veins like floodwater finding a cellar. The mountain shudders to its roots. Ten thousand lantern-bearers on the steps feel it and keep climbing, because nobody sane stops a rite for weather.`)+((G.f.a1_intent=="home")?(P(`For one instant, in the column of rising souls, you can see it — the way between, open, real, exactly as the dead man promised, the heat of a hundred passages pouring outward to somewhere with porch lights. It is RIGHT THERE. And it is closing as the furnace dies, and the only way to hold it open is wound around the wrist of a husk on the floor, and you let it close, because the price was always somebody, and you have spent a year becoming someone who knows that.`)):(""))+P(`The breach has to be held NOW, or the flood takes the veins and the mountain comes down with everyone on it.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Weave the breach shut — fabric, not knots, the furnace's own dying threads turned back as warp and weft.`,req:()=>(G.realm>=3),do:()=>{G.f.a2_breach="clean";note("It takes everything you have and it HOLDS — a patch of new gold in the mountain's old silver, woven so clean the dragon vein barely changes key. You will sleep for two days. The mountain will never know it almost died.");},go:"a2c12_open"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Hold it and SHOUT — you planted help at this threshold, and harvest season cuts both ways.`,req:()=>(G.sho>=2),do:()=>{G.f.a2_breach="helped";note("You hold the tear with raw threads and screaming arms until the door bursts: a blind sweeper who hears the Weave, an inner-court genius who keeps his word. None of you could have done it alone. All of you together barely do.");},go:"a2c12_open"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Hold it with your own two hands and pay what it costs.`,do:()=>{G.f.a2_breach="burned";G.hp=Math.max(1,G.hp-10);G.f.a2_scar=true;note("-10 HP. You stitch yourself across the breach and let the flood burn through you on its way to nowhere. It holds. Your left palm will carry a thread-of-gold scar down the lifeline forever — the mountain's receipt.");},go:"a2c12_open"}]};